Package: fipsd
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         systemd
Recommends: nftables
Suggests: libfipsnative-dev
Description: FIPS mesh network daemon (C port)
 FIPS is a distributed, decentralized network routing protocol for mesh
 nodes connecting over arbitrary transports (UDP, TCP, and Nostr-mediated
 rendezvous). fipsd is the nostrc C port of the daemon: encrypted
 peer-to-peer links with automatic key management, a TUN-based IPv6 mesh
 interface, a .fips resolver and a Unix control socket.
 .
 This package ships the daemon, its systemd units (fipsd, fips-dns and the
 opt-in fips-firewall nftables baseline), the fips system group that gates
 the control socket, and an example configuration seeded to
 /etc/fips/fips.yaml on first install.

Package: fips-gateway
Architecture: any
Depends: fipsd (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         iproute2
Description: FIPS outbound LAN gateway
 Linux IPv6 LAN-to-mesh gateway using libnftables NAT and proxy NDP.
 Reads the gateway block in /etc/fips/fips.yaml. The systemd service is
 opt-in: configure the pool and LAN interface before enabling it.

Package: libfipsnative0
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: client library for the fipsd native datagram API
 libfipsnative is a plain-POSIX C client for the fipsd native datagram API:
 programs link it to open flows over the mesh through the daemon's
 SOCK_SEQPACKET API socket, with no dependency on the daemon's runtime
 or protocol core.
 .
 This package contains the shared library.

Package: libfipsnative-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libfipsnative0 (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: client library for the fipsd native datagram API (development)
 libfipsnative is a plain-POSIX C client for the fipsd native datagram API.
 .
 This package contains the header, the static library and the pkg-config
 file.
